# E-346: Let $A=\{1\leq a_1< a_2<\cdots\}$ be a set of integers such that $A\backslash B$ is complete for any finite subset $B$ and $A\backslash B$ is not complete for any infinite subset $B$. (Here 'complete' means all sufficiently large integers can be written as a sum of distinct members of the sequence.) Is it true that if $a_{n+1}/a_n \geq 1+\epsilon$ for some $\epsilon>0$ and all $n$ then\[\lim_n \frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}=\frac{1+\sqrt{5}}{2}?\]
